{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/pulls/362","id":4946907156,"node_id":"PR_kwDORu27H88AAAABJtvQFA","html_url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/362","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/362.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-hax/eta-mu/pull/362.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/issues/362","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/pulls/362/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/pulls/362/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/issues/362/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/eta-mu/statuses/fa117fba0b761f8aa655e26c2ae8675b1af178cd","number":362,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(review): add bounded archive admission and publication contracts","user":{"login":"riatzukiza","id":10676925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc2OTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10676925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza","html_url":"https://github.com/riatzukiza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The review producer mixed candidate/model execution with App signing and native publication. This branch depends on #361 and adds portable publication decisions, physical archive admission, bounded native reads, independent Git reconstruction, immutable Muse verification, and Clio-backed intent coordination. Privileged end-to-end publication remains incomplete.\n\nThe latest source `c72928f632f50f832b5dc54a732697d15e0cc4d2` adds a bounded fixed NBB worker using canonical Clio replay and stream-slot CAS in one precreated authoritative partition. Only a fresh admitted post-started acknowledgment may mint a private process-local one-use effect capability. Restart/replay/recovery grant no fresh effect authority. Host-clock re-admission and atomic consumption bind that capability to the intended request.\n\nIndependent review reproduced public capability minting, caller-mutated recovery injection, numeric-fold/SHA-lock mismatches and a pathname-replacement race. Retained causal RED/GREEN repairs the first boundaries; the last required the proper canonical owner API. The exact candidate dependency `riatzukiza/clio@5fad794de1a9e23d6e5aaad42eaa933be1c070be` checks device/inode identity on the actual descriptor under its owning lock before ledger read/append. ETA carries exact decimal strings from BigInt stat through guarded reads, append and retry. All 27 selected installed kernel source/config files match that revision. Candidate composition does not advance accepted root pins.\n\nFinal source-frozen intent tests pass **18 tests / 88 assertions**. Full CLI **194 / 587**, workflows **11 / 199**, owning/scoped lint and release pass with zero warnings. Actual independent worker replacement replay observes a different inode, retains both files empty, returns the Clio identity-mismatch error and issues no capability. One-use capability, exact visible recovery and stale-context probes pass. Original failed test mechanisms and intermediate source results remain distinct; an additional baseline harness failed and supplies no new RED. Opaque public uncertainty-receipt round-trip after post-started failure remains unproven.\n\nEarlier collector source remains exact-source evidence: native PR files are collected in both enrolled tuple/run passes with bounded fixed routes, exact count 0–3,000, required metadata, unique filenames and explicit missing/null/string patches. Collection passed 30/224 and 20 actual pure parity cases. Its public GET probe read 90 files twice over nine pages per pass (20 requests, 1,981,780 response bytes); 17 patches were missing. Complete API rows/pages never prove complete patch text. The probe observed remote ab03 and does not supply tested or hosted proof for the successor.\n\nOriginal G, executed caller source, runtime tools/input proof and complete source/verifier composition remain missing. Native API H/current M/time joins and historical payload HMAC cannot supply those claims. Production registry remains absent/refusing. Native review POST/readback/status, effective grants, protected installation/default adoption and successor hosted qualification remain unfinished. Earlier successful Sandbox at b265 remains bound to its exact merge/source; producer success with skipped review jobs supplies no review or publication.\n\nEvidence: `.ημ/review-evidence/trusted-publication-intent/execution.json`, 809-capture digest `69c3ffe6776f476cd409421d4b1a4df250e57d1569a8685d3afa452f5db248d8`, immutable metadata attempt `2197cbde7e3e9a155d00b8a1efb4650485911b8ae765b2fa4129aebcafdf2419`. All 309 card states/planning and four ledger prefixes verify. The publisher stays **in_progress / Codex**. The prospective native receipt validates; whole history retains **71 invalid rows / 118 errors**. Native findings, review cooldowns and Codex UNKNOWN reset remain obligations. Auto-merge stays off; consumer pins and paused CMS/Cephalon remain unchanged.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added portable board snapshots with paths relative to a selected root, while preserving planning metadata.\n  * Added read-only review metadata collection, source reconstruction, evidence verification, and bounded archive validation.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved checksum validation and snapshot error handling; invalid or unverifiable evidence is rejected.\n* **Chores**\n  * CI workflows no longer require private-repository access or publication credentials.\n* **Tests**\n  * Expanded coverage for credential-free workflows, review evidence, archive validation, publication decisions, and snapshot portability.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified that producer evidence does not establish publication qualification or confirm publication.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:33:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T02:32:04Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"462feb7d3a32aa9f82409ea5bcddaf24c2376b5b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"riatzukiza:feat/trusted-review-publication-20261021","ref":"feat/trusted-review-publication-20261021","repo":{"id":1401249220,"node_id":"R_kgDOU4VdxA","name":"eta-mu","full_name":"riatzukiza/eta-mu","owner":{"login":"riatzukiza","id":10676925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc2OTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10676925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza","html_url":"https://github.com/riatzukiza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gith